{%- comment -%}
  AJ How — what this site is, for somebody who just arrived from an ad.

  IT SITS BELOW THE DEAL, NOT ABOVE IT, and that placement is the whole design
  decision. The mobile fold is already completely spent on the Yoink — image,
  label, price, saving, countdown, add to cart. Putting an explainer above it
  pushes the countdown and the buy button off-screen, so paid traffic would be
  paying for a click and then hiding what it came for. The hero already
  explains a great deal by SHOWING: a labelled deal, a large saving, a running
  clock. What it cannot answer is "does this happen again tomorrow", which is
  the question that turns a one-time buyer into the repeat visitor this
  business actually runs on.

  THE SECOND STEP DOES NOT SAY THE PRICE GOES BACK UP, and that was deliberate.
  The fact is true and worth having — most discount stores fake it with a
  permanently inflated compare-at, and this one genuinely restores, which is a
  verifiable honesty claim. But as a headline it makes EXPENSIVE the default
  state, which quietly devalues 2,300 other products and a Bargain Bin that is
  permanently 25% off. "Then it's gone and tomorrow it's something else" buys
  the same urgency and spends the line on the return visit instead of the loss.
  The price-restores fact lives on the About page, where trust is the job.

  THE THIRD STEP EXISTS TO ANSWER "IS THIS WHOLE SITE ONE PRODUCT?" — the other
  thing a cold visitor genuinely wonders, and the reason they would otherwise
  leave rather than scroll.

  IT DESCRIBES THE BIN, NOT THE STORE, and the first draft got this wrong in a
  way worth recording. "Everything else, permanently 25% off"
  reads as the whole catalogue being discounted. Measured: the bin holds 38
  products against 2,392 active ones — 1.6% of the store — and every one of
  them is at EXACTLY 25%, never more. A shopper who takes that sentence
  literally and then browses a category finds 2,354 products at full price,
  which is the kind of small overclaim that costs more trust than the sentence
  ever earned.

  Copy is lifted from the welcome email rather than written fresh, so the site
  and the inbox say the same thing in the same voice.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
-%}

<div
  class="aj-how color-{{ s.color_scheme }}"
  style="padding-block-start: {{ s.padding-block-start }}px; padding-block-end: {{ s.padding-block-end }}px;"
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div class="aj-how__inner page-width">
    {%- if s.definition_term != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The dictionary device, not a paragraph. It is the same line the About
        page and the social teasers use, so anyone arriving from an ad gets
        continuity rather than a second explanation of the same word.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Real spaces between the spans, not just CSS margins. The margins render
        the gap correctly for anyone looking, but a screen reader concatenates
        the text nodes — verified in the live DOM, where it came back as
        "YOINK(v.)to grab something great" with no breaks at all.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <p class="aj-how__def">
        <span class="aj-how__term">{{ s.definition_term | escape }}</span>
        {% if s.definition_pos != blank %}
          <span class="aj-how__pos">{{ s.definition_pos | escape }}</span>
        {% endif %}
        <span class="aj-how__gloss">{{ s.definition_gloss | escape }}</span>
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      THE LIST IS NOT RENDERED AT ALL WHEN EVERY STEP IS BLANK.

      Each step was already guarded individually, which meant clearing all six
      fields left an EMPTY `<ol>` behind — invisible, but still collecting the
      definition's bottom margin above it and still announced as a list with no
      items. Since the cadence calendar took over the explaining, that is the
      normal state of this section rather than an edge case, so it is worth
      being exact about: the band is now the definition and nothing else.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign has_steps = false
      if s.label_1 != blank or s.body_1 != blank
        assign has_steps = true
      endif
      if s.label_2 != blank or s.body_2 != blank
        assign has_steps = true
      endif
      if s.label_3 != blank or s.body_3 != blank
        assign has_steps = true
      endif
    -%}

    {%- if has_steps -%}
    <ol class="aj-how__steps">
      {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
        {%- liquid
          case i
            when 1
              assign label = s.label_1
              assign body = s.body_1
            when 2
              assign label = s.label_2
              assign body = s.body_2
            when 3
              assign label = s.label_3
              assign body = s.body_3
          endcase
        -%}
        {%- if label != blank or body != blank -%}
          <li class="aj-how__step">
            {%- comment -%}
              The numeral is aria-hidden: an ordered list already announces
              position, and "one. one a day." is the kind of duplication that
              makes people switch a screen reader off.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="aj-how__num" aria-hidden="true">{{ i }}</span>
            {%- if label != blank -%}
              <span class="aj-how__label">{{ label | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if body != blank -%}
              <span class="aj-how__body">{{ body | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ol>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    A CYAN BAND, because the first version was correct and characterless — a
    numbered list in grey on white, which is every SaaS "how it works" section
    ever shipped and says nothing about this shop.

    Cyan is the one brand colour doing no work anywhere else: teal holds the
    header, purple the footer, yellow the story band below. It also breaks up a
    homepage that runs white from the deal all the way to the story.

    INK ON CYAN, NEVER CYAN AS TYPE. aj-brand.css measured cyan at 1.66:1
    against white, which fails WCAG 1.4.3 at any size as text. As a background
    under ink it is the opposite problem — comfortably past AA — which is the
    same reason the yellow is only ever a fill.
  */
  .aj-how {
    background: var(--aj-brand-cyan, #5cd8f8);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
  }

  .aj-how__inner {
    max-width: 62rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  /* ---- the definition, now the loudest thing here ----------------------- */

  /*
    THE DEFINITION IS THE HERO, not a caption above a list. It is the one line
    that explains the brand's own name, it is already the device used on social
    and on the About page, and set at display size it does more work than three
    steps of body copy.
  */
  /*
    NO BOTTOM MARGIN. The gap below the definition now lives on the steps list
    instead — see `.aj-how__steps` — so that when there are no steps there is no
    gap either. Carried here, the margin would hold open 2.25rem of empty cyan
    under a band that is otherwise three lines tall.
  */
  .aj-how__def {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .aj-how__term {
    display: block;
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 3.25rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  /* Sits under the word like a dictionary entry rather than beside it. */
  .aj-how__pos {
    display: block;
    margin-block: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.62;
  }

  .aj-how__gloss {
    display: block;
    max-width: 34ch;
    margin-inline: auto;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* ---- the steps -------------------------------------------------------- */

  .aj-how__steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    /* The space between the definition and the cards. It belongs to the cards,
       so it disappears with them. */
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-how__steps {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 1.25rem;
    }
  }

  /*
    Each step is a card in the ink, not a bullet on the band. Three solid blocks
    read as deliberate objects; three lines of text on a colour read as a caption
    that overflowed.
  */
  .aj-how__step {
    position: relative;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.35rem 1.35rem;
    border-radius: var(--aj-tile-radius, 8px);
    background: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  /*
    The numeral is a chip that overlaps the card's top edge — the small piece of
    deliberate untidiness that stops three rectangles looking like a table.
    Yellow on ink is 11.17:1, the brand's loudest legal pairing.
  */
  .aj-how__num {
    position: absolute;
    top: -0.7rem;
    left: 1.2rem;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    transform: rotate(-4deg);
    background: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .aj-how__label {
    display: block;
    margin-block-end: 0.4rem;
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .aj-how__body {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    opacity: 0.82;
  }

  /* ---- motion ------------------------------------------------------------ */

  /*
    TWO DIFFERENT ANSWERS, BECAUSE PHONES HAVE NO HOVER.

    Desktop gets a lift on hover — motion that answers an action, which is the
    only kind this codebase ships. Touch gets a scroll-driven entrance instead:
    the cards rise as they come into view, which is the closest thing to
    interactivity a finger can trigger without tapping something.

    THE TWO NEVER FIGHT OVER A PROPERTY. The entrance owns `translate` and the
    hover owns `scale` — CSS's independent transform properties, specifically so
    a scroll-driven animation holding its end state cannot be clobbered by a
    hover rule, and vice versa. Written as one `transform` on both, whichever
    fired last would win and the cards would jump.
  */
  .aj-how__step,
  .aj-how__num {
    transition: scale 0.18s ease, box-shadow 0.18s ease, rotate 0.18s ease;
  }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    .aj-how__step:hover {
      scale: 1.02;
      box-shadow: 0 14px 28px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.22);
    }

    /* The chip straightens up as you arrive, then leans back when you leave. */
    .aj-how__step:hover .aj-how__num {
      rotate: 2deg;
      scale: 1.1;
    }
  }

  /* Touch feedback: a press should feel like a press even with nothing to tap. */
  .aj-how__step:active {
    scale: 0.985;
  }

  /*
    Scroll-driven, so no JavaScript and no IntersectionObserver. Guarded twice:
    @supports for browsers without a view timeline, which simply see the
    finished state, and reduced-motion for people who asked not to have this.
  */
  @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      .aj-how__step {
        animation: aj-how-rise linear both;
        animation-timeline: view();
        animation-range: entry 5% cover 30%;
      }

      @keyframes aj-how-rise {
        from {
          opacity: 0;
          translate: 0 18px;
        }

        to {
          opacity: 1;
          translate: 0 0;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    /* Same move as the desktop rule: the gap belongs to the cards, so it goes
       when they do. Left on the definition it reopened the dead space this
       change exists to close, on the one screen where it costs the most. */
    .aj-how__steps {
      margin-block-start: 1.75rem;
      gap: 1.4rem;
    }

    .aj-how__gloss {
      font-size: 1.0625rem;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ How it works",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Sits below the Yoink, above the Bargain Bin. Copy matches the welcome email on purpose — the site and the inbox should say the same thing."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Definition" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "definition_term", "label": "Word", "default": "Yoink" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "definition_pos", "label": "Part of speech", "default": "(v.)" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "definition_gloss",
      "label": "Definition",
      "default": "to grab something great half a second before the person next to you."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Step 1" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_1", "label": "Label", "default": "One a day" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "body_1",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "We dig up one genuinely good thing and drop it at a price that feels like a mistake."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Step 2" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_2", "label": "Label", "default": "24 hours" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "body_2",
      "label": "Text",
      "info": "Deliberately does not say the price goes back up — that makes expensive the default. See the note at the top of the section file.",
      "default": "Then it's gone, and tomorrow it's something else."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Step 3" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_3", "label": "Label", "default": "The Bargain Bin" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "body_3",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "A bin of items marked 25% off that rotates every week."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "color_scheme", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Color scheme", "default": "scheme-1" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Padding" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-start", "label": "Top", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 40 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-end", "label": "Bottom", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 40 }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "AJ How it works" }]
}
{% endschema %}
